description:
Configure a Global Shared Pipeline Library in Jenkins and create a job to test it. 

1. Go to Manage Jenkins > System. 
2. In the 'Global Trusted Pipeline Libraries' section, add a library with:
   - Name: 'jenkins-shared-lib'
   - Default version: 'master'
   - Retrieval method: Modern SCM
   - SCM: Git
   - Project Repository: 'https://github.com/jenkins-infra/pipeline-library.git'
3. Save the configuration.
4. Create a new Pipeline job named 'shared-lib-test'.
5. Configure the job with a Pipeline script that imports the library:
   @Library('jenkins-shared-lib') _
   pipeline {
       agent any
       stages {
           stage('Verify') {
               steps { echo 'Library loaded' }
           }
       }
   }
6. Save the job.

